      "id": 1,
      "text": "Muddy is known in the Cheyenne language as Heóvonėheo'hé'e, which translates to Muddy Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muddy%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Northern Cheyenne bands once used the Muddy Creek area for seasonal encampments and communal buffalo hunts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/muddy_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Muddy Creek, the area's central waterway, means yellow-paint-creek in the Cheyenne language.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/muddy_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Muddy lies along the Tongue River watershed within the broader Powder River Basin of southeastern Montana.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/muddy_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The landscape around Muddy features expansive grasslands with scattered cottonwood groves and timbered ridges.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/muddy_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Local wildlife in the Muddy area includes pronghorn antelope, mule deer, and white-tailed deer.",
